            "question_id": 14120,
            "is_toggle_on": true
          },
          {
            "id": 789,
            "sort": 2,
            "name": "Overview",
            "value": "<div data-page-id=\"YP3XdinBZozo9Qx3V4elcqv1gBd\" data-lark-html-role=\"root\" data-docx-has-block-data=\"false\">\n<div class=\"ace-line ace-line old-record-id-J54Bd9WyBo5JXexlS98lOQVQgjh\">Overall, the library has undergone a major transformation from a traditional library to a modern facility with numerous new amenities. The most significant changes include the removal of the multimedia and reading sections, which have been replaced by new areas such as a lecture room, a computer room and a caf&eacute;.</div>\n</div>",
            "question_id": 14120,
            "is_toggle_on": true
          },
          {
            "id": 790,
            "sort": 3,
            "name": "Body 1",
            "value": "<div data-page-id=\"YP3XdinBZozo9Qx3V4elcqv1gBd\" data-lark-html-role=\"root\" data-docx-has-block-data=\"false\">\n<div class=\"ace-line ace-line old-record-id-OdvpdM4GKo08lBxoblmlxeOvgre\">Two decades ago, on the upper side of the old layout, there were three distinct sections: CDs, videos and computer games on the left, children's books on the right, and adult non-fiction books opposite to them. Following the renovation, this area has been significantly modified, with the multimedia section being converted into a storytelling area with sofas, while the children's book section has been replaced by a lecture room. Currently, the adult fiction books area, which was originally situated in the center-left area, and a new information desk occupy the space that previously housed non-fiction books.</div>\n</div>",
            "question_id": 14120,
            "is_toggle_on": true
          },
          {
            "id": 791,
            "sort": 4,
            "name": "Body 2",
            "value": "<div data-page-id=\"YP3XdinBZozo9Qx3V4elcqv1gBd\" data-lark-html-role=\"root\" data-docx-has-block-data=\"false\">\n<div class=\"ace-line ace-line old-record-id-KrFrdj7RGosZKGxmzB8lr0o6gGh\">Initially, at the bottom of the original plan, there was a reading room for newspapers and magazines on the left and an enquiry desk for tickets and returns on the right. After the changes, these have been replaced by a computer room and a caf&eacute; respectively. At present, new features have been added to the current layout, including self-service machines, an information desk, and a dedicated area for reference books, making the library more modern and self-service oriented.</div>\n</div>",
